# Sidebar & Routing

## SideNav Structure
`src/components/SideNav.jsx` has two nav arrays:

```jsx
// Primary nav — shown in the scrollable middle section
const navItems = [
  { icon: 'dashboard', label: 'Dashboard', to: '/', filled: true },
  // icon: Material Symbols name
  // filled: true = use FILL:1 on active state
]

// Bottom nav — shown above the footer divider
const bottomItems = [
  { icon: 'settings', label: 'Settings', to: '/settings' },
]
```

## Adding a Nav Item
```jsx
// In navItems or bottomItems:
{ icon: 'person', label: 'Team Roster', to: '/roster' }
```
Then add the route in `App.jsx`:
```jsx
import TeamRoster from './pages/TeamRoster'
// Inside the Layout route:
<Route path="roster" element={<TeamRoster />} />
```

## Active Link Styling
`NavLink` handles active state automatically. The pattern is:
```jsx
className={({ isActive }) =>
  `flex items-center gap-3 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-body-sm transition-all ${
    isActive
      ? 'text-secondary bg-secondary-fixed font-bold'
      : 'text-on-surface-variant hover:bg-surface-container'
  }`
}
```
For `filled` icons, apply `fontVariationSettings: "'FILL' 1"` when `isActive`.

## TopNav
`src/components/TopNav.jsx` — fixed, `z-50`, `h-16`. Contains:
- Brand name: `L&D Insights` (never change without design approval)
- Search input: `rounded-full`, `hidden sm:block`
- Notification bell with red dot badge
- Avatar initials (not an image — uses `<span>` with `"A"`)

## Layout Shell
`src/components/Layout.jsx` manages sidebar open/close state for mobile:
```jsx
const [sideNavOpen, setSideNavOpen] = useState(false)
```
The `<Outlet />` renders the current page inside `<main className="flex-1 p-gutter overflow-y-auto">`.

## Mobile Behavior
- Sidebar: `translate-x-full` → `translate-x-0` via `open` prop
- Overlay: `fixed inset-0 bg-black/30 z-30 md:hidden` — clicking closes sidebar
- Menu button in TopNav calls `onMenuToggle` which toggles `sideNavOpen`

## Route Guards
No auth is implemented. All routes are publicly accessible. To add protection:
```jsx
// Wrap in a <RequireAuth> component that redirects if !isAuthenticated
<Route path="admin" element={<RequireAuth><AdminPage /></RequireAuth>} />
```
